uestId":"req_011CfZQ544LWqQ5KP6ufPxPu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"08e433f1-aa6b-4cc9-84bb-92a6f2068be4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:37:01.007Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"08e433f1-aa6b-4cc9-84bb-92a6f2068be4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"832e1406-bbbf-40c1-a1f3-aab8fe479c03","agentId":"af8d90b8a1ac4b5a4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012J2W7CwGS4iokq284odyRW","type":"tool_result","content":"K-TOOLS-11 world-editor-viewport spans three literatures (3D manipulation UX, large-world editing, mesh editing) and provides C-EDVIEW on which ~25 domain tools depend, so modeling/paint work shares the contract's change queue. Separately, ED.COLLAB.binaries (large binary storage) sits in ci-cd-automation while VCS choice, locking and sparse workspaces sit in collaboration-version-control, though depot layout cannot be decided apart from binary storage. \n-- Move ED.WORLD.blockout and ED.WORLD.mesh-paint to a mesh-editing expert (or asset-cook-processors alongside CNT.COOK.geometry-ops); move ED.COLLAB.binaries to collaboration-version-control with ci-cd-automation as contributor. \n\nK-TEST-2 Gate validators are not independent and often do not exercise the property validated. About 28 gates have owner and validator in the same workstream (security-engineering and privacy-data-protection sit in quality). Circular pairs: gate-canaries vs agent-boundary; QA.FUNC.soak vs PRF.MEM.footprint; scale-content vs asymptotics; release-criteria to compat-corpus to prechecks. The sealed holdout is validated by QA.SIM.golden-traces, which cannot show implementers cannot read it; the mutation gate is validated by fuzzing, not seeded weak tests. Gates carry no pass criterion. \n-- Extend gate schema to {capability, validator, kind, criterion (metric, threshold, evidence-bundle item)}. Require validator owner workstream different from capability owner workstream and forbid 2-cycles and triangles. Re-pair holdout to a red-team read attempt (agent-redteam plus BLD.CI.sealed-suites) and mutation-gate to seeded weak-test injection. Move security-engineering and privacy-data-protection to assurance. \n\nK-NET-4 Auth-ticket and service-identity validation is stated in two capabilities with different owners (NET.TRANS.crypto and NET.SESS.auth), and the handshake in three (NET.ARCH.versioning, NET.SESS.handshake, the transport crypto handshake). Nothing says where the transport handshake ends and the session handshake begins, or who binds the ticket to the transport session key. \n-- NET.TRANS.crypto covers only channel encryption and key establishment (remove ticket/service-identity from its text). NET.SESS.auth is sole owner of ticket validation and channel binding. Add an authenticated-channel state with key-binding token to C-NETLINK. NET.ARCH.versioning keeps policy only. \n\nK-GAMEPLAY-2 accessibility's purpose claims 'motion and photosensitivity options', but no capability implements them. The only photosensitivity row is QA.CERT.photosensitivity (late cert testing). There is no runtime flash/luminance/red-flash limiter or reduced-flash mode, no authoring-time flash analysis of VFX, cutscenes and UI, and no contract by which VFX, sequencer and UI honour such a setting. \n-- Add UI.A11Y.photosensitivity (owner accessibility; contributors post-color-hdr, vfx-particles, cinematics-sequencer, ui-architect, certification-compliance) for the runtime limiter plus the C-A11YRT setting. Add a flash-analysis tool and a CNT.VAL validator on cooked sequences and VFX. Keep QA.CERT.photosensitivity as sign-off. \n\nK-SIM-9 GPU fluid solvers are E while the particle and grid fluids they run are M. The radar entry is titled 'Particle & GPU fluids' but lists only particles and grid, so PHY.FLUID.gpu has no fallback or revisit trigger. \n-- Set PHY.FLUID.gpu to M and list it on the radar entry, or merge it into particles/grid. \n\nK-PERF-3 Structural contracts that fix world-scale asymptotics are frozen at M1 on 2D indie games, but asymptotic declarations and stress worlds are first gated at M5/M6. Their validators are circular: M5 gates scale-content validated by asymptotics, and M6 gates asymptotics validated by scale-content. A scaling flaw found at M5 forces a breaking change to frozen contracts consumed by most skills. No scale probe runs before freeze. \n-- Add an M1 gate for PRF.METH.asymptotics (declaration) validated by PRF.BENCH.scale-content, plus an M1 scale-probe (1e6 entities, 1e4 cells, 64 cores, fitted slopes) as a precondition to freezing C-FRAME, C-FLOW, C-SPATIAL, C-VIEW and C-SIGNIF. Break the M5/M6 circularity by giving scale-content an independent oracle. Make 'asymptotic line declared' a freeze condition for every contract. \n\nK-ARCH-1 render-2d-vector, post-color-hdr, vfx-particles, material-system, C-VT, C-COLOR, C-TEMPORA | In minimal/2D configurations non-optional edges pull the 3D render stack into 2D and UI-only builds: render-2d\nK-ARCH-2 skills.json profiles/targets, configurations minimal-client and online-3d-server, referenc | Scale-down is proven only as closure, not minimality. Membership is profile 'all' or match, and most skills ar\nK-ARCH-3 C-SNAPSHOT, C-REP, C-PREDICT, C-SAVE, C-SRVDATA, C-SIGNIF, CORE.REFL.attributes, CORE.ECS. | Each stateful subsystem must declare its state independently to snapshot, replication, prediction, save, serve\nK-ARCH-4 PHY.ARCH.validation, ANM.ARCH.validation, AUD.ARCH.validation, GAM.AI.validation, RES.MGMT | Oracle suites are owned twice: physics/animation/audio 'oracle suite' capabilities belong to the implementing \nK-ARCH-5 robustness-fuzzing, functional-automation-soak, simulation-validation, render-validation ( | Four process skills author every conformance suite: functional-automation-soak 35 contracts, robustness-fuzzin\nK-ARCH-6 ARCH.ORG.ownership-ledger, ARCH.ORG.agent-continuity, ARCH.ORG.write-sets, ARCH.ORG.proven | The coordination machinery is software (lease/lock server with fencing tokens, per-path access-class enforceme\nK-ARCH-7 milestones M1-M3 contracts_frozen; indie-2d-client, minimal-client, fighting-2d-rollback-c | M2 claims indie-2d/minimal/fighting-2d shipping on PC, console, mobile and web while the non-optional contract\nK-ARCH-8 NET.PRED.lagcomp, PHY.ARCH.rewind, ANM.RT.pose-history, GAM.SYS.hit-detection, GAM.SYS.pro | Lag compensation/server rewind is split across four skills (collider history in physics, pose history in anima\nK-ARCH-9 PHY.ARCH.materials, C-ENV, GAM.SYS.impacts, WLD.ENV.terrain-materials, audio-content-runti | The surface-type taxonomy is owned by physics-architect but is the shared key for terrain layers (C-ENV surfac\nK-ARCH-10 CORE.FRAME.sim-schedule, CORE.FRAME.access-model, C-FRAME, docs/00 section 6 | Same owner says both that ordering is derived from declared access by one scheduler and that the simulation sc\nK-ARCH-11 visual-debugging-tools, editor-architect, C-DEVUI, C-AUTOMATION | A runtime skill shipping in client, headless and server builds is parented to the tool lead editor-architect, \nK-ARCH-12 engine-architect, ARCH.ORG.escalation, C-A11Y | engine-architect has 29 direct children and is sole arbiter for intra-workstream, cross-workstream and party-l\nK-SEC-1 ARCH.ORG.sensitive-paths; ARCH.ORG.skill-lifecycle; ARCH.ORG.human-gates; critics.json; un | The agent control plane is not a protected write set. It covers the ledger and access classes, critics.json an\nK-SEC-2 untrusted-inputs.json; NET.TRANS.local-network; NET.SRV.community-hosting; NET.SESS.server | Parsers of hostile bytes have no registry entry, so the fuzz and limits proof never covers them. Missing input\nK-SEC-3 untrusted-inputs.json; XC.SEC.agent-boundary; XC.SEC.agent-redteam; ARCH.PROD.upstreaming; | The agent-input class omits tool and MCP server responses and descriptions, persisted agent memory and hand-of\nK-SEC-4 milestones.json M0, M2, M4; XC.SEC.agent-redteam; XC.SEC.dev-trust; XC.SEC.server-validati | 22 of 30 XC.SEC capabilities are never named in a milestone gate. These include agent-redteam (agents write co\nK-SEC-5 security-engineering; XC.SEC.agent-boundary; XC.SEC.key-custody; XC.SEC.dev-trust; XC.SEC. | One process skill both defines product security and owns the security of the agent program itself (agent bound\nK-SEC-6 untrusted-inputs.json cloud-saves; GAM.SAVE.integrity | Cloud saves are labeled semi-trusted-signed. A client-held signature does not authenticate against the device \nK-SEC-7 XC.SEC.hardening; C-SIGN; PLAT.SRV.host-os; NET.SRV.community-hosting | No capability covers microarchitectural side channels and co-tenancy: Spectre-class mitigation policy for ship\nK-SEC-8 XC.SEC.tamper; anti-cheat-integrity; C-INTEGRITY; security-runtime | Anti-tamper and DRM boundary is owned by a process skill with no code territory. Executable self-integrity, la","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"319ddb83-cad4-4ede-a602-839b95ac5bc5","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:37:01.099Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08e433f1-aa6b-4cc9-84bb-92a6f2068be4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
